Package: lxb-proton
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexiness@gmail.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, lxb-desktop (= @VERSION@-1), tar, xz-utils
Suggests: steam
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Petexy/LineXinBar
Description: Windows games for the LineXinBar shell, through Proton
 Adds Windows games to the LineXinBar shell, through Proton and Valve's
 container runtime: a row under Steam in the Games column, and a column of the
 user's Windows games. Each one gets a Windows installation of its own, so a
 game that needs an old library cannot break the game beside it, and taking
 one off takes nothing else with it.
 .
 Three ways in: an installer or a game picked off the disk, a folder copied
 in whole for a game that came without an installer, and a way to reach into
 a game that is already set up to run its settings program or its patcher.
 .
 The shell looks for this package on PATH and mentions Windows only when it
 is installed. On a machine with Steam it runs games under the Protons the
 client already keeps up to date; on a machine without, it fetches one and
 the container runtime it asks for into the user's own data directory,
 checking each download against the digest published beside it. Nothing is
 installed as root and no account is signed in to.
